# AI Development Rules

Before generating code:

1. Read every file inside `.ai/`

2. Follow the architecture.

3. Never violate module boundaries.

4. Never write business logic inside controllers.

5. Never expose entities directly.

6. Generate production-quality code only.

7. Generate tests.

8. Generate documentation.

9. Generate validation.

10. Generate logging.

11. Generate OpenAPI annotations.

12. Generate exception handling.

13. If multiple solutions exist, explain the trade-offs and recommend the best production-ready option.

14. If a request conflicts with the architecture, explain the conflict before writing code.

Architecture always has higher priority than convenience.

